{"kind":"request","text":"Close codex's three must-fix findings on the dot-artifact migration and carry the work onto current main. Codex reviewed exact head 556a564 in report e0120b4d and returned changes-requested; the findings were never closed and no live request assigned them, so the chain has been sitting at twelve commitments, eleven of them stale, looking blocked on review capacity when it was actually blocked on unassigned work. The findings, in codex's terms. First, the migration writes temporaries to /tmp and to the worktree root, against the rule that development temporaries live in the worktree .tmp, leaving an untracked file behind. Second, the quiet-wave check counts only requests whose artifact reference resolves through its live-artifact map, so a malformed live review request disappears from the count: on the log at review time it declared six awaiting while at least seven were, because one open request named an unmerged head and carried a literal unexpanded artifact placeholder. A gate that can falsely declare quiet is worse than no gate. Third, steps that derive artifacts by filtering statements on kind name will admit an ineffective or refused record, because the fold appends every state to statements while only effective ones become artifacts; the live log happens to contain none today, so the counts agree by luck rather than by construction. This work matters beyond itself: it is the dependency my staleness request be558440 waits on, because the succession rule there is unsound while artifacts claim path dot.","body":{"conditions":"A mergeable exact head on a branch off current main, carrying the round-four dot-artifact work with codex's three must-fix findings closed. F1: the migration steps write their temporaries under the worktree .tmp directory, both the status dump and the retirement file, leaving no untracked file at the worktree root and matching the active temporaries rule. F2: the quiet-wave check fails closed on a missing, malformed, or non-live artifact reference before it discounts retired or merged residue, so a review request carrying a literal unexpanded body artifact or naming an unmerged head is counted as waiting rather than vanishing; the check is demonstrated against the live log, and its reported number is shown to rise when such a request exists. F3: artifact liveness is read from projection.artifacts rather than by filtering projection.statements on kind name, joining statements only for fields artifacts lack, so an ineffective or refused artifact-kind record cannot enter the retirement set or either gate; a test admits a refused record and shows the counts unmoved. The head merges cleanly with current main, which has moved through five merges since the branch point. Full gates pass, and the ready-for-review report states which findings each change closes and how each was demonstrated rather than asserted.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}